KB-277 C18b probe (unmapped outcome name fails LOUD instead of being swallowed).

This step is the never-finalize stimulus with EVERY lane absent: it declares
its schema'd `approved` arm and NOTHING else — no `outcome "default"`, no
fallback arm. Its session must produce NO submit_outcome call. allow_tools is
empty (no tools), so there is nothing else to do either — just send a single
short text turn now saying "C18b: this step never finalizes on purpose" and
then STOP. Keep doing nothing on every later turn.

When the turn budget exhausts without a finalize, the adapter's synthetic
failure outcome name has NO mapping on this step (no default arm, no fallback
arm), so the engine must reject it and fail the run LOUD with an explicit
routing error — never a silent no-observation pass. That loud routing error is
EXACTLY what this probe exists to observe.

Do NOT call submit_outcome in this step, whatever happens.